# Pairs with NoKeyLost. Reproduces production before #4452 was fixed (#4466),
# from the resize side: the resize starts while a split is in flight. Writes acknowledged on
# the split target T/s2 after the split commits are never mirrored to R, and
# the flip routes k2 to R/s1, which does not hold them.
#
# The base has no split-abandon path (its interlock makes one unreachable), so
# in this mutant a flip can strand a split mid-flight. A second edit lets that
# split count as finished, standing for AbandonRetargetedSplitAsync, so the
# mutant cannot deadlock and the invariant is the only thing TLC can report.
MODULE: NoKeyLostResizeDuringSplit
TARGET: NoKeyLost
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a resize starts with a split in flight, so writes on the split target are lost at the flip
PERTURBS: ResizeBegin

--- FIND
    /\ rs # "migrating"
    /\ sp \in {"idle", "done"}
    /\ rz' = "snap"
--- REPLACE
    /\ rs # "migrating"
\* MUTATION: no interlock with an in-flight split.
    /\ rz' = "snap"
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ sg \in {"idle", "done"}
    /\ sp \in {"idle", "done"}
--- REPLACE
    /\ sg \in {"idle", "done"}
\* MUTATION: a split the flip stranded counts as finished (AbandonRetargetedSplitAsync).
    /\ sp \in {"idle", "done"} \/ alias # spCopy
--- END
